# PXQU tier map 'pxqu-flashnext-4xp100-granite-ub1024': Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Uncensored (arch qwen4exp).
# Derived from pxqu-flashnext-4xp100-150k-ub1024.tiers (the parent). ONE change class:
# mid-depth gate/up experts stepped pxq3 -> pxq2 so the seat fits FOUR P100s of which
# dev0 is SHARED WITH THE GRANITE PRODUCTION SERVER (global CUDA cards 0,1,5,6;
# card 0 carries granite at ~8.4 GiB resident, only ~7.9 GiB free; card 3 = 1080Ti
# is NOT part of this seat).
#
# TARGET  4x Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB = global cards 0,1,5,6 (CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID,
#         NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,5,6), -fa on, -c 150016 (ledger max ~163840),
#         -b 2048 -ub 1024, -ctk f16 -ctv f16, per_layer_token_embd pinned to CPU
#         (-ot 'per_layer_token_embd\.weight=CPU'), head on dev3 (global card 6), NOT dev0.
# EXPERTS 37.285 GiB, avg 2.6514 bpw, hist {'pxq2': 88, 'pxq3': 56}.
#         (parent: 42.168 GiB @ 2.9986 bpw, {'pxq2': 38, 'pxq3': 106})
# WEIGHTS GPU-resident 41.210 GiB (parent quant measured 46.093 on the same shapes);
#         file ~91.9 GiB (the 50.66 GiB Q8_0 PLE stays CPU/host-resident).
# LEDGER  per-card, NOT aggregate (-ts partitions BYTES, not layer counts). Constants
#         are the MEASURED ones from the 2026-08-28 campaign: compute 570 MiB/ordinary
#         card + 980 MiB head card at ub1024 (does NOT scale linearly with ub, head
#         does not scale with ctx), ~280 MiB ctx/cuda overhead, KV 24576 B/token
#         (12 of 48 layers hold KV: 3,7,..,47), >= ~1.2 GiB kept free per card because
#         decode allocates transients beyond the init-reported compute buffer.
#         At c=150016 (KV 3516 MiB total), contiguous split 6/15/15/12 layers:
#           dev0 (card 0, GRANITE seat, 7.9 free)   6 lay  w  5079 + kv  293 + 570 + 280 = 6222 used, ~1.7 free
#           dev1 (card 1)                          15 lay  w 12612 + kv 1172 + 570 + 280 = 14634, 1.6 free
#           dev2 (card 5)                          15 lay  w 12612 + kv 1172 + 570 + 280 = 14634, 1.6 free
#           dev3 (card 6, HEAD+embd/output 1007)   12 lay  w 11897 + kv  879 + 980 + 280 = 14036, 2.3 free
#         -ts 5079,12612,12612,11897  (per-card weight MiB; confirm the run's own
#         "Setting default device in layer N" lines and rebalance from the log, never
#         from memory). ub2048 is NOT attempted: the head-card compute buffer carries
#         the n_vocab*n_ubatch logits slab and the 5-card campaign already measured the
#         miss; ub1024 is the owner floor and the measured sweet spot.
#
# WHAT CHANGED vs PARENT (the ONLY change):
#   ffn_gate_exps + ffn_up_exps stepped pxq3 -> pxq2 on layers 19..43 (50 rules,
#   -100.0 MiB per tensor, -4.883 GiB total). Layers 0..18 were already pxq2 in the
#   parent (its depth x kind proxy rates early gate/up least sensitive); layers 44..47
#   keep pxq3 to protect the last ~4 layers. All 48 ffn_down_exps stay pxq3 - down is
#   UNPROTECTED in this arch (no ffn_norm, no output_norm; the hc mixer is the only
#   normalisation, so down's error enters the wide residual unrescaled). NEVER drop a
#   down below pxq3. hc_* stays F16 everywhere - NEVER quantize hc_* (q8_0 would evict
#   96 calls/token from ggml_cuda_small_gemv_f16 onto emulated dp4a on P100 and perturb
#   the gate scaling the wide residual). Attention/ssm_out/shexp stay pxq4 and
#   attn_k/attn_v/indexer stay q8_0 as in the parent: stepping mid-depth pxq4 -> pxq3
#   was evaluated and HELD IN RESERVE - it frees only 262 MiB total (0.26% of a card)
#   for a precision cut on the every-token attention path; the gate/up step alone
#   reaches the ledger with >= 446 MiB min-slack on top of the 1.2 GiB/card reserve.
#
# CORRECTION 1 (carried from parent) -- hc_*_down / hc_*_up stay F16. See parent for
#   the full mechanism (ggml_cuda_small_gemv_f16 gates on src0 F16, ne1 in [2,512]).
#
# CORRECTION 2 (updated for this seat) -- the budget is re-solved for dev0 being a
#   GRANITE-SHARED card: any -ts that treats card 0 as a full 16 GiB card will OOM the
#   production seat. dev0 total (weights+kv+compute+ctx) is capped at ~7.1 GiB against
#   ~7.9 GiB free. Re-check nvidia-smi before every boot; do not carry a -ts forward
#   from memory.
#
# NOT USED: an importance matrix. Owner decision -- measured a net negative on our
#   quants. Do not add one.
#
# Consumed by llama-quantize --pxq-universal (flags BEFORE the positional filenames).
#
# FIX (carried from parent, wake 2): explicit f32 rules for every tensor with
#   ne0 %% 32 != 0 -- ssm_conv1d [4,10240] x36, ple_conv1d [4,10240] x1, ssm_a [48] x36,
#   ssm_dt.bias [48] x36. Leaving these RULELESS DOES NOT LEAVE THEM ALONE: with no rule
#   they fall through to the PXQU default type MXFP4 (llama-quantize.cpp:1499), a
#   block-32 codec, and GGML_ASSERT(n_per_row %% kBlockSize == 0) ABORTS the run at
#   tensor 59/1224 after 57 GiB written. Preflighted against the real tensor geometry
#   of the Uncensored PXQU header before this build was started.
#
